"Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+2.2% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 145 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are roughly flat over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the bottom of its 52-week range, 17% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 21% and a beta of 1.02, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.47 vs 5y 1.02), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $460.7M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 36% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 83% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $43.50 (margin of safety -192%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 45%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Real Estate peers: EV/EBITDA 23.2 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 27% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 2.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 14 covering analysts target $152 on average, 20% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.5%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.58).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.50x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 57%.","ROE of 6% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 2.1% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.9x net debt to EBITDA ($1.1B of cash against $35.0B of debt), with interest covered 4.3x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.7% over 3 years, 14.6% over 5 years and 14.9% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 14%).","Free cash flow has compounded 33.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 11.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.1x depreciation (3.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 99%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 2 sales over the past year, net $7.4M sold.","It returns 3.1% a year to shareholders (3.4% in dividends).","The share count has grown 4.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 28 consecutive years, raising it 16.9% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 2,802 employees, each generates about $3.1M of revenue, 1.4x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 13.3% a year across its filed history.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $2.7M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $66K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":37.0,"head":"Red flag: priced 192% above its fair value of $43.50.","pros":["Revenue grew 14.6%/yr over 5y","14 analysts' mean target $152 (+20%)","Returns 3.1% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 192% above fair value of $43.50","ROIC 5.1% vs WACC 8.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 4.9x","EV/EBITDA 23.2x vs sector 16.3x"],"flags":["Priced 192% above its fair value of $43.50"],"vc":{"base":43.5,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":43.5,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.4534,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":24.44,"ev_ebitda":16.258,"pfcf":17.4416,"pb":1.3433,"roic":0.0405,"gross_margin":0.551,"fcf_margin":0.1749,"div_yield":0.0475}},"ticker":"PLD","date":"2026-11-27"}